Appendix C: Perturbation Bound for Contractions

Theorem C.1. Let (X,d) be a complete metric space and T: X \to X a contraction with coefficient \gamma<1 and unique fixed point x^*. Suppose \hat{T} is an operator with \sup_{x} d(\hat{T}(x), T(x)) \le \epsilon. Then for any sequence x_{n+1} = \hat{T}(x_n),

\limsup_{n\to\infty} d(x_n, x^*) \le \frac{\epsilon}{1-\gamma}.

Proof. Standard: d(x_{n+1}, x^*) \le d(\hat{T}(x_n), T(x_n)) + d(T(x_n), T(x^*)) \le \epsilon + \gamma d(x_n, x^*). Iterating gives d(x_n, x^*) \le \gamma^n d(x_0, x^*) + \epsilon \sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \gamma^k. Taking \limsup yields the bound. ∎

