Appendix E: Mixture Property of Dobrushin Coefficient

For completeness, we prove the inequality used: for a finite mixture of Markov kernels K = \sum_i p_i K_i where \sum_i p_i =1 and p_i are constants (independent of the state), the Dobrushin coefficient satisfies \delta(K) \le \max_i \delta(K_i).

Proof. \|K(x,\cdot)-K(y,\cdot)\|_{TV} = \|\sum_i p_i (K_i(x,\cdot)-K_i(y,\cdot))\|_{TV} \le \sum_i p_i \|K_i(x,\cdot)-K_i(y,\cdot)\|_{TV} \le \sum_i p_i \delta(K_i) \|x-y\|_{TV} \le (\max_i \delta(K_i)) \|x-y\|_{TV}. Taking sup over x,y gives \delta(K) \le \max_i \delta(K_i). ∎

